<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Batum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus-campaign">Caucasus campaign</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batumi">Batum</a> was signed on 4 June 1918 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the new republics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> after the collapse of the Transcaucasian Federation. It forced Armenia to cede large territories, leaving it a small landlocked state of about 10,000 square kilometres around Erivan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-sevan">Lake Sevan</a>, crowded with refugees. It was overturned by the Ottoman defeat and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-mudros">Armistice of Mudros</a> in October 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-batum.jpg" alt="Treaty of Batum" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peachy1621 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batum_Treaty.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
